@meeting promo.result
// FX28 (2026-10-26, the user's playtest notes; lead 38's plan D): with PROMO_BEATS_ON the summons is your result, first
// thing the next workday (08:15, Calder's glass office). She tells you you've passed and gives you the Technician's
// badge; the pip is the Captain's, this afternoon. One reply, which she remembers (C2 stores promo.reply 1-3 by the
// choices' order: proud, surprised, about time; keep it). If she had to come and find you (08:30), it plays where you
// are. Drafted by FX28 for SW2 to polish.
title: Your result
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder gave you your result: you passed. You're a Works Officer now, Technician, Tier 2. The Captain pins your pip this afternoon.
== lines
calder > you: Door. Thank you. Two minutes.   [gesture]
calder: Your scrubber. Four bolts, one filter, no notes from me.
calder: Result: passed. You're an Officer from today. Technician, Tier 2.
calder: Your badge. Pin it level. I'll know if it isn't.
? choice
* Thank you, Chief. I'll do it properly.   rel:calder+2
  calder: You already do. That's what the badge is for.   [nod]
* Really? This soon?   rel:calder+1
  calder: Really. Soon isn't the measure. Ready is. You're ready.
* I wondered when you'd say so.   rel:calder+1
  calder: Hm. So did Torres. Out loud. Daily.   [nod]
calder: The pip isn't mine to give. The Captain pins it this afternoon, observation room. Clean uniform.
calder: Tier 2 work on the board from tomorrow. Tonight, after dinner, I walk you to your cabin. 4-23.
calder: Go on, then. They're waiting outside.
